            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "উদ্দেশ্য — uddeshyô — \"a purpose; an aim\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "এই মিটিংয়ের উদ্দেশ্য কী? ei miṭingyer uddeshyô kī? What is this meeting for?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "উদ্দেশ্য (uddeshyô) is Sanskrit uddeśya, the thing one points at or has in view (Monier-Williams). Bengali uses it for the purpose behind a plan or a meeting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
